{
  "comments": [
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "706a0982_9dccf336",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T00:54:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this will break pKVM if the \"restricted\" bit does anything more than provide information to the gunyah backend. i think originally you changed the MemoryRegion accessors to check this bit and error if protected memory was accessed and that seems to be gone now so there is technically no problem, but i\u0027m worried it will cause confusion later\n\ncan you add a new hypervisor capability to guard this?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d267d63_49dcd9f1",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858345
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T15:51:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now it only provides bit to gunyah backend. This bit would eventually be used to know whether this memory needs to be backed by restricted_memfd, too.",
      "parentUuid": "706a0982_9dccf336",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e789447_20fc7d1e",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858345
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T15:52:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With that in mind, I don\u0027t think hypervisor capability is necessary here.",
      "parentUuid": "8d267d63_49dcd9f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bf99e99_9a9d8bc0",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T22:55:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i get that, but, as i said, i think it will cause confusion once restricted_memfd is added, especially if some pKVM code in crosvm decides to start using the bit, then we\u0027ll have a mess to untangle\n\n`protection_type.isolates_memory()` is not ever going to imply restricted_memfd (at least not in any time frame worth considering at this point)",
      "parentUuid": "1e789447_20fc7d1e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86f91f5e_6acee2c7",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858345
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T23:10:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e `protection_type.isolates_memory()` is not ever going to imply restricted_memfd (at least not in any time frame worth considering at this point)\n\nWhat would the decision factor be to use restricted_memfd, assuming kernel can support it? I was thinking the decision is same was what Gunyah needs today.",
      "parentUuid": "4bf99e99_9a9d8bc0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "951ab5a8_79c7c8b6",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T23:20:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m imagining that the presence of the hypervisor capability is how we communicate that the kernel supports it. Do you have a different idea?",
      "parentUuid": "86f91f5e_6acee2c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dd70294_1fb01691",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858345
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T23:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree hypervisor capability for restricted_memfd is right way to communicate whether kernel supports it. When would crosvm take advantage of this capability and for which memory regions?",
      "parentUuid": "951ab5a8_79c7c8b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a30ca5c3_81b9069e",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858345
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T23:35:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do you have a different idea?\n\nI don\u0027t have other different idea for communicating the kernel support. I think there\u0027s a two part decision. Part of the decision is kernel support (via a hypervisor capability). The other part I thought would just be \"isolates_memory()\"",
      "parentUuid": "2dd70294_1fb01691",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e116e29e_046d89a5",
        "filename": "aarch64/src/lib.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-14T23:36:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think anyone has a full design for restricted_memfd in crosvm and ofc it is still not in upstream so might change. To start with I think adding a hypervisor capability that is somewhat gunyah specific and does exactly what you want here would be easiest. This is all crosvm internals, so we can freely evolve it later.",
      "parentUuid": "2dd70294_1fb01691",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 305,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 305,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6a5227c838d6b145748066348a5b49a3de68a2aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
